- User expects strict layered architecture and robustness standards: avoid exposing entities in APIs, enforce DTO validation, add DB indexes/constraints for query and uniqueness patterns, include idempotency metadata in events, and maintain production-ready consistency across ProductService files.
- User wants strict DTO boundaries (no entity leakage at API/service boundaries), service-owned business logic (especially stock math), repository focused on persistence, explicit cache invalidation on mutations, typed result models instead of object, and consistency/performance in search and pagination handling.

